{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall not wrong a stranger.</b> In verbal oppression; <b>nor shall you oppress him</b> — in monetary robbery. In several places it is written in the Torah, and the Holy One, blessed be He, warned concerning the stranger, because the stranger finds himself alone in a foreign land, and therefore he is called גר from the language of גרגיר, a single grain found alone at the tip of a branch. People demean him and do him harm; therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said: do not think that he has no one to plead his cause, for I am the One who pleads his cause and takes vengeance on those who oppress him. And this is why He gave the reason: ״ואתם ידעתם את נפש הגר כי גרים הייתם בארץ מצרים״ — and you know the soul of the stranger, for you were strangers in the land of Egypt. He did not say 'and you know the stranger' but rather 'the soul of the stranger,' meaning: you know that every stranger's soul is lowly within him, and he has none to whom he can lift his eyes except Me; therefore I have compassion upon him, just as I had compassion upon you when you were strangers in the land of Egypt. And He joined to him the widow and the orphan, because all of them are faint of strength and people take lightly the matter of doing evil and oppressing them. And behold, their tears are ever-present, for the gates of tears are not shut; therefore a person must be careful with them — to do good and show kindness to them, whether with his person or with his money. And so the prophet mentioned (Isaiah 58:7): ״הלא פרוס לרעב לחמך״ — is it not to share your bread with the hungry? And he further mentioned (ibid.): ״ותפק לרעב נפשך״ — and offer your soul to the hungry. If you have bread to give him, give; and if not, offer your soul — that is, prepare yourself to provide him contentment with words. And the reason He mentioned the expression 'every widow' — even a wealthy one who owns property — is because her tears are ever-present and her soul is bitter within her."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:02.052501231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}